# Copy to `.secret-denylist` (gitignored) and list your own private terms here.
#
# One term per line, case-insensitive, plain substring match. `#` starts a
# comment. This file itself is COMMITTED, so it must only ever contain
# placeholders — the real list belongs in `.secret-denylist`, which never
# leaves your machine.
#
# Typical entries:
#   my-ssh-alias
#   my-server-hostname
#   203.0.113.10
#   my-private-key-name
#   client-project-codename
#
# Then run:  npm run scan:secrets
#
# Example placeholders (all harmless, keep or delete):
example-alias
example.invalid
203.0.113.10
